#question(title: [Collection of antiderivatives], shrink: true)[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  Let $display(f)$ be a positive, continuous
  function with domain $RR$.  \
  We know two ways to describe a collection
  of antiderivatives:
  + $display(G(x) + C)$ for $C in RR$, where
    $G$ is any one antiderivative.
  + The collection of functions
    $display(F_a)$ for $display(a in RR)$,
    where
     $
       F_a (x) = integral_a^x f(t) d t
     $

  These two collections are not always the
  same. Why not? Are they the same for some
  functions $f$? When are they the same?

  #v(2.5cm)
  #h(1fr) #emph[Hint:] #h(1em)
  #link("https://tinyurl.com/137antiderivatives")[#goto-button[https://tinyurl.com/137antiderivatives]]
]
